SUMMARY:[AI ADJUSTED] cycling — Keep the morning open-water swim (1\,500
 –2\,000m at easy effor
DESCRIPTION:Keep the morning open-water swim (1\,500–2\,000m at easy effo
 rt) as the primary session\; reduce the afternoon ride to 60–70 min / 25
 –30km at 120–150W rather than 75–80km — cap total daily training l
 oad and cut the ride short if HR exceeds 145 bpm.\n\nReason: This is only 
 the second weekend back from illness and stacking a full OW swim plus a 75
 –80km ride risks an excessive single-day load spike that could trigger r
 elapse or excessive fatigue heading into the Treviso 10K build weeks.\n\nA
 I coaching 2026-08-08
